      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/man-la-yahduruhu-al-faqih:4:92:1",
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/92/5454",
      "text": [
        " :\n\"دَخَلْتُ عَلَى مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ اِبْنِ اَلْحَنَفِيَّةِ وَ قَدِ اُعْتُقِلَ لِسَانُهُ فَأَمَرْتُهُ بِالْوَصِيَّةِ فَلَمْ يُجِبْ\"\nقَالَ \"فَأَمَرْتُ بِطَسْتٍ فَجَعَلْتُ فِيهِ اَلرَّمْلَ فَوُضِعَ فَقُلْتُ لَهُ خُطَّ بِيَدِكَ فَخَطَّ وَصِيَّتَهُ بِيَدِهِ فِي اَلرَّمْلِ وَ نَسَخْتُ أَنَا فِي صَحِيفَةٍ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5454 - Abd Al-Ṣamad ibn Muhammad narrated from Hanan ibn Sadir from his father, from Abu Ja'far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), who said:\n\"I entered upon Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Al-Hanafiyya, and his tongue had become paralyzed.\nI instructed him to make his will, but he did not respond. So, I ordered a basin to be brought and filled it with sand.\nI said to him, 'Write with your hand,' and he wrote his will in the sand with his hand, and I copied it onto a scroll.\""
        ]
      }
    },
